I've been playing with this myself.  I've got nethack to not strip the eighth
bit.  In prisym.c, you need to #undef ASCIIGRAPH.  I'm not sure yet if this
is the best way to do it, but it seems to work.  Unfortunately, xterms refuse
to display the characters from 129 to 161.  Unfortunately
this doesn't leave me quite enough characters to do everything I want.

I will definitely produce a 14x24 font of some sort with patches to make
it work.  No promises on when I will be done.  Another hacker here has been
prodding me towards writing a real X11 interface (non-xterm).  This would
be ideal, and you could do lots of nifty things, but I really *HATE* the
X11 library.  We'll see.

